  "known_history": [
    {
      "finding": "The renderStatus requirement in hotkey_host service/handle is already present in version 1.0.28, and absent from the previously changed 1.0.19 hotkey_host file.",
      "version": "1.0.28",
      "commit": "8d4f5980dce6adcfa63ff45bc8af6e93c99a9a56",
      "date_utc": "2026-10-21T04:51:52Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/ARISAKAHIKARI/RA2-Toolbox-Build/blob/8d4f5980dce6adcfa63ff45bc8af6e93c99a9a56/source/assist/source/hotkey_host.h"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The complete pre.3 Registry implementation, including sampledOnly filtering of physical press events, already exists in 1.0.39-pre.7. Ordinary keys depend on WM_HOTKEY in that version as in 1.0.43.",
      "version": "1.0.39-pre.7",
      "commit": "7b920372a8eb872bfafc1ba03da15028da425acf",
      "date_utc": "2026-10-29T09:04:38Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/ARISAKAHIKARI/RA2-Toolbox-Build/blob/7b920372a8eb872bfafc1ba03da15028da425acf/source/assist/source/hotkey_routes.h"
    }
  ],
  "conclusion": [
    "No removal of ordinary-key polling between v1.0.43 and 1.0.46.4 can be attributed to hotkey_routes.h: the entire file is byte-identical.",
    "No newly introduced renderStatus gate between these versions can be attributed to hotkey_host.h or desiredHotkeyMode: the relevant files/functions are identical.",
    "RegisterHotKey failure dropping a binding is also unchanged, as are registration synchronization, WM_HOTKEY dispatch and the per-module message loop.",
    "pre.4 negative controls demonstrate existing failure conditions (absent WM_HOTKEY / unavailable display state), not the commit that newly caused the user regression.",
    "The remaining plausible regression is a changed producer, readiness state or sampling dependency feeding the unchanged gates; this history review alone does not establish that cause."
  ]
}
